# This file previously contained a private key that has been removed for security.
# The original key was committed to version control and MUST be rotated (revoked and reissued).
#
# To provide a TLS private key, use one of the following approaches:
#   1. Set the TLS_KEY_PATH environment variable to point to your key file
#   2. Set the TLS_KEY environment variable with the PEM-encoded key content
#   3. Place your own generated key at this path (do NOT commit it to source control)
#
# Generate a new self-signed key for development:
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout server.key -out server.crt -days 365 -nodes -subj '/CN=localhost'
